# Forever scoring (every class)

Item facts come from Wowhead Forever ingest. All nine classes are on this model. Re-score one class at a time after a rule change. Do not `reemit_all.py` from stale JSON.

**Order:** damage (spec primary) first, then survivability (sta/armor below 60), then endurance (mana keep-up, less than stam). Level 60 is raw raid weights. Max 3 unique names + 1 notable per slot.

## Do not change weights unless asked

`weights.json`, the numbers in `score.py` `weights_at_level()`, and `ScoringWeights.generated.lua` stay until the user explicitly asks for a retune. A piece ranking first because of an existing weight is the model working.

Priest, mage, and warlock `dpsWeightRanged` is **7** (same scale as a warrior melee weapon). These classes cast, then wand. **White Obsidian Wand** (274425) is rank 1 ranged at 39 for mage, priest, and warlock because 7 × 41.47 DPS wins the slot. Do not lower that weight to bury it. Greater Magic Wand stays the client 17.5 DPS. Warlock schools and Enhancement Tank armor (0.20, 0.40 below 60) stay as they are.

## Coordinates, sets, tooltips, scrapes

- A hunt gets a coordinate whenever a real spot exists (quest start, dungeon or raid entrance, named creature, vendor, object). Do not invent one. Unsourced has none until a source exists. Ruins of Lordaeron is Undercity map 1458 at 71.6, 11.4. Patch with `index_coordinates.py --ids`. Do not full-emit (`emit()` rewrites the whole file).
- Every re-score counts set bonuses (Embrace of the Viper, Rotmender's Raiment, any `(N) Set`) via `apply_embrace_package` / `apply_rotmender_package`. Pieces scored alone are the wrong list.
- Tooltip layout stays Wowhead line order. Slot and type are one double line, and so are Damage and Speed. The client set is spliced in place. Drop Chance, Requires Level, and Sell Price stay in the tail. If the stored tip already has `(N) Set`, do not add the client set again. Random-suffix greens keep the jackpot tooltip.
- A Wowhead Forever scrape **inserts new ids only**. Do not refresh existing `items.json` facts from the tooltip cache (that reverted Erudite to a stale blue). Then recheck every item still marked Unsourced: if the listview or tooltip now names a quest, a vendor, or Dropped by, fill that source and `index_coordinates.py --ids` those ids. Do not call a still-empty row a world drop.

## Random-enchant jackpot is BiS

Rank a random-enchant green on the **best suffix it can roll** (top of that suffix’s range), not the expected value across every suffix.

- Superior Shoulders of Agility at 22 is **+6–7 Agi** (~9.5%). If that roll would be #1 in the slot, it **must** appear as BiS #1.
- `suffixChance` / the log hint tell the player the roll is slim. Chance never buries the hunt.
- Implemented in `pipeline/scripts/score.py` `best_variant` (`ROLL_POLICY="bestRoll"` ranks on jackpot).

## Leveling survivability (below 60)

Leveling is not raid min-max. Stamina, health, and armor beat a naked +1 primary-stat upgrade.

- Example: at 22, **Brawler’s / Trapper’s Leather Tunic** (8 Agi + stam / str / int) beat **Panther Armor** (9 Agi, no stam).
- `score.py` `weights_at_level()` multiplies sta / health / hp5 ×3 and armor ×2 when `level < 60`.

## Leveling endurance (below 60)

Survivability also means having and keeping mana. Call this **endurance**. It is less important than stamina, but it matters for most classes (paladin seals/heals, shaman shocks, hunter shots, caster drinks).

- `weights_at_level()` multiplies int / spirit / mp5 / mana ×2 when `level < 60` (stam is ×3).
- Level 60 uses the raw raid-scale weights. Forever level-60 guides may pin later; until then `GQ_NO_GUIDES=1`.

## Warrior tank is physical

Warrior Protection does not score spell power or healing. A glove with +SP / +healing (Silvered Gauntlets) is not BiS even if the stam is fat. If it also has defense, it is the **notable** for that slot — not rank 1.

## Shaman Enhancement Tank is a hybrid

Like paladin Protection: 1h + shield, stamina/armor/defense first, then Rockbiter melee threat, then Earth Shock / Lightning Shield spell threat. Not dual-wield (Forever has no shaman DW). `enhancement_tank` in `weights.json`.

## Refreshed Forever tooltips (score from these)

Stats come from the refreshed Wowhead Forever tooltip (`refresh_forever_tips.py`), then a re-score. Do not full-ingest to refresh tips (that replaces `sources.json` for id ≥ 200000). Client pins stay: Coldflame, Silverlaine, Wolfsbane required level 20. Kaleidoscope resist 5 stays. Emit the audit **before** rescoring so recovered ids leave `FOREVER_MISSING`.

- The Equip line `Increases damage and healing done by magical spells and effects by up to N` is stored as **both** heal=N and damageDone=N. Do not strip it. Do not collapse it to spell power only. `forever_stats` folds damageDone into spell power so it is not counted twice. Holy uses the heal half. Mages (heal weight 0) use the damage half. An unequal "healing up to X and damage up to Y" stays heal=X, damageDone=Y (Staff of Westfall: 48 and 16). Skip party lines. A green `+N Spell Power` line is spell power only.
- **Required level is the tooltip `Requires Level`, never item level.** A stated level greater than 1 is never replaced. Fang of Magmatus is 13. Every item with **no** required level (or Wowhead's stub of 1) is assumed to be a quest reward, or some other gated source, until looked up. Find the quest on Wowhead Forever and set the required level to the **minimum** level that can pick up that quest (`Requires level N`; item XML `<json>` reqlevel, not `jsonEquip`, not the scaling minLevel). Several quests: take the lowest. The item-level floor is only a stand-in until that lookup is done. Fang is not pinned over Golemheart.
- Cloaks, rings, necks, trinkets, and held items with `kind` `?` are `Misc`. `kind` `?` is not equippable.
- Weapon headers are labels only. If a staff is rank 1, main-hand rank 2 is the one-hand that off-hand rank 1 pairs with. A second staff may sit at rank 3 with a higher score than rank 2.
- Fishing and skinning are Profession. Container loot uses the Container filter. An active filter hides source types that have no checkbox. `GetItemInfo` names of the form `Item 23173` are not names; use the stored fact or audit name.

## Mage Battle Mage

Caster who swings. Specs: `battlemage_frost` (the hunt), `battlemage_fire`, `battlemage_arcane`. Spell power of that school first. Stamina base 0.15 (slightly above frost 0.1). Weapon `dpsWeight` 0.35. Coldflame Saber and Blade of Silverlaine stats are the Forever **client** tooltip, pinned in `client_item_overrides.json`. Do not sync the Wowhead nether tip back over them. The saber’s 98 Fire vs Frozen is every swing during a freeze (`FROZEN_MELEE_UPTIME` 25% frost, 15% fire/arcane). On an imbued weapon, printed stats stay the normal colors and only the imbue effect is grey. Do not repeat that effect. Add `Use: Combine the <base weapon> and <scroll>.` (`CLIENT_IMBUE` in `Data.lua`).
